    <section class="intern-body" aria-label="Internship Information">
      <div class="intern-inner">
        <div class="intern-header-row">
          <div>
            <h2 class="intern-heading">Now Accepting Fall 2026 Applicants</h2>
            <p class="intern-sub">We are accepting applications for Fall 2026! Please submit your resume for consideration.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="connect.html" class="btn btn-green intern-resume-btn">Submit Resume</a>
        </div>
        <p class="intern-body-text">Our internship opportunities focus on integrative wellness, social justice, community care, and nonprofit development. We aim to provide a hands-on learning experience that allows interns to explore and grow their leadership abilities, expertise, and interests within the nonprofit sector.</p>
        <p class="intern-body-text">All roles are hybrid, with 80% of the work done virtually and 20% in-person, including attending wellness experiences to gain firsthand insight into the industry. Interns will commit 8-10 hours per week for 6-9 month placements, and have the option to earn college credit or receive a monthly stipend.</p>
        <p class="intern-body-text">We have hosted more than 30 interns from DMV-area universities including Howard University, University of Maryland, Trinity Washington University, American University, The Catholic University, and Morgan State University.</p>
        <div class="intern-types">
          <div class="intern-type">
            <h3 class="intern-type-heading">Healing Justice Internship</h3>
            <p class="intern-type-body">Supports community-centered healing work by integrating trauma-informed practices, restorative approaches, and equity-driven programming for individuals and communities impacted by systemic harm.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="intern-type">
            <h3 class="intern-type-heading">Integrative Wellness Initiatives Internship</h3>
            <p class="intern-type-body">Engages holistic wellness strategies that connect mind, body, and community health through culturally responsive practices, prevention, and sustainable self-care tools.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="intern-type">
            <h3 class="intern-type-heading">Marketing &amp; Communications Internship</h3>
            <p class="intern-type-body">Develops storytelling, digital content, and outreach strategies that amplify mission-driven work, strengthen community engagement, and expand organizational visibility.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="intern-type">
            <h3 class="intern-type-heading">Organizational Development Internship</h3>
            <p class="intern-type-body">Builds internal systems, strategy, and capacity by supporting program design, evaluation, and infrastructure that advance long-term sustainability and impact.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main><!-- /#main-content -->

